cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this scientific code or analysis snapshot, cite this exact version."
title: "PrecisionPhage: leakage-controlled phage-host prediction and fixed-bank cocktail scoring"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Samadhiya"
    given-names: "Jaivardhan"
    affiliation: "West Valley College"
version: "2026.10.15"
date-released: 2026-10-15
repository-code: "https://github.com/JaivardhanSamadhiya/frontiers_submission"
url: "https://github.com/JaivardhanSamadhiya/frontiers_submission"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Scientific code and compact data for leakage-controlled phage-host prediction,
  frozen source-transfer tests, and retrospective scoring of published
  fixed-bank Escherichia cocktail assays. Original frozen results are preserved
  alongside explicitly retrospective controls, feature ablations and crossed
  host-cluster/composition uncertainty sensitivities. This research snapshot
  does not establish clinical efficacy or de novo cocktail-selection benefit.
keywords:
  - bacteriophage
  - phage-host interaction
  - machine learning
  - data leakage
  - external validation
  - reproducibility
